{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "metadata": {
    "id": "pw8-deep-bass",
    "name": "DEEP BASS",
    "author": "Patchwork Eight Engineering",
    "description": "A clean, simple, warm sub-anchored bass part -- built to hold down the root under a pad and an arp without competing with either. Deliberately plain: a sine fundamental, an exact-unison (not detuned) triangle for a little harmonic body, and a sine sub an octave down for real low-end weight -- no detune beating, since beating that's pleasant in a pad reads as mud at bass frequencies. A dark, low-resonance filter (900Hz) keeps it controlled. Only a light Saturation for analog warmth; no chorus or delay, and only a short, light Reverb (mix 0.12, decay 1.2s) -- a washy bass smears the low end for everything mixed on top of it, so this stays comparatively dry and short. No modulation routes -- the bass is the one part in these arrangements deliberately left completely static so the ear has one fixed point of reference while the pad and arp move.",
    "category": "bass",
    "moods": ["warm", "clean", "grounded"],
    "genres": ["ambient", "score"],
    "tags": ["bass", "sub", "arrangement-part"],
    "createdAt": "2026-08-10T00:00:00Z",
